# sideman — a tour of the dial, two bars per rhythm, for a clip that shows the
# disc RE-STAMPING itself as the selector moves.
#
# The point of the tour is the thing a grid cart cannot show: the number of
# slots on the disc CHANGES with the rhythm. Watch the track layout when it
# reaches SHUFFLE (four beats of triplets, 12 slots) and WALTZ (three beats,
# also 12) — everything else carries 16.
#
# The cart self-plays: `motor = true` on frame 1, so there is no SPACE to press.
# Each rhythm also brings its own tempo, so two bars is not a fixed number of
# frames; ~150 frames per step is a comfortable two bars at the middle tempos
# and never cuts a bar off at the fast end.
#
# Starts on FOXTROT 4 BEAT (index 4, the one every organ player used), so the
# tour walks forward from there and wraps around the whole dial.
down 150 RIGHT
up   152 RIGHT
down 300 RIGHT
up   302 RIGHT
down 450 RIGHT
up   452 RIGHT
down 600 RIGHT
up   602 RIGHT
down 750 RIGHT
up   752 RIGHT
down 900 RIGHT
up   902 RIGHT
down 1050 RIGHT
up   1052 RIGHT
down 1200 RIGHT
up   1202 RIGHT
